    "text": "Hauptseite\nFoundations of Cybersecurity 1\nBen Stock\nNews\nUpdate on tutorials and exercises\nWritten on\n22.10.26\nby Nicolas Gundall\nDear all,\nSince today's lecture is cancelled, we are missing the main content that would normally be discussed in the tutorials. We will thus convert the next set of tutorials (23.10. and 26.10) into office hours. This means that no new content will be presented; instead you are welcome to ask your…\nRead more\nDear all,\nSince today's lecture is cancelled, we are missing the main content that would normally be discussed in the tutorials. We will thus convert the next set of tutorials (23.10. and 26.10) into office hours. This means that no new content will be presented; instead you are welcome to ask your tutor questions about the course contents so far. If you do not have any questions, you do not need to attend. If you choose to come to an office hour, please arrive at the regular starting time, because the tutors may leave early in case all questions are answered.\nFurthermore, we have to make some adjustments to the scheduling of exercise sheets and python tasks. To prevent confusion, here is the current release schedule:\nWeek\nNew python tasks? (Tuesdays)\nNew exercise sheet? (Thursdays)\n19.10. to 25.10. (current)\n✅️\n❌️\n26.10. to 1.11.\n✅️\n✅️\n2.11. to 8.11.\n✅️\n✅️\n9.11. to 15.11.\n✅️\n✅️\n16.11. to 22.11.\n❌️\n✅️\nFrom then on\n✅️\n✅️\nCancellation of tomorrow's lecture\nWritten on\n21.10.26\nby Ben Stock\nDue to an important meeting I have to attend, we will have to cancel tomorrow's lecture. We soon update the schedule on the CMS start page, but you can assume that we will have a lecture on November 19.\nChange in tutorials: update your preferences\nWritten on\n13.10.26\nby Nicolas Gundall\nDear all,\nwe've been notified that the tutorial we scheduled on\nFridays 10-12\ncollides with the MfI1 lecture for many students. Tutorial preferences also indicated that very few students could attend this slot. Consequently, we have decided to\nmove this tutorial to Mondays 12-14 instead\n.\nPlease…\nRead more\nDear all,\nwe've been notified that the tutorial we scheduled on\nFridays 10-12\ncollides with the MfI1 lecture for many students. Tutorial preferences also indicated that very few students could attend this slot. Consequently, we have decided to\nmove this tutorial to Mondays 12-14 instead\n.\nPlease make sure to update the tutorial preferences on your personal status page accordingly. You can adjust your preferences until the end of this Thursday's lecture.\nFirst lecture tomorrow\nWritten on\n12.10.26\nby Nicolas Gundall\nHello everyone,\nwe have now updated all course information for this year, which can be found on the main page. The first lecture will take place\ntomorrow (Tuesday) from 10:15 to 11:45 in GHH (E2 2)\n. It will start with further information regarding the organization of the course, and then go into…\nRead more\nHello everyone,\nwe have now updated all course information for this year, which can be found on the main page. The first lecture will take place\ntomorrow (Tuesday) from 10:15 to 11:45 in GHH (E2 2)\n. It will start with further information regarding the organization of the course, and then go into the first course topics. See you all then!\nFoundations of Cybersecurity 1\nAbout the course\nThis is a mandatory course of all Bachelor Cybersecurity students. Any other students may be unable to take the CP associated with the lecture, please check the\nLSF\nto see if your course of study is listed.\nIn this course, students will learn foundational security principles, the basics of cryptography, receive an introduction to networks and network security, and explore privacy-preserving mechanisms. Additionally, students will acquire programming skills in Python.\nBy the end of the course, students should be able to define security goals and become familiar with the most common attack scenarios.\nTime and Location\nThe lecture is held on Tuesday 10:15 - 11:45 (in E2 2 (GHH)) and on Thursday 14:15 - 15:45 (in E1 3 HS0.01).\nThe\ntentative\nschedule is as follows:\n13.10. Organization, Information Security Goals, Legal Aspects in Germany\n15.10. Basics of Cryptography 1 (Historic & Block Ciphers)\n20.10. - Python 1 (Arithmetics & Strings)\n22.10. -\nno lecture\n27.10. - Python 2 (Boolean Logic, Lists, Basic Loops)\n29.10. - Basic of Cryptography 2 (Hashes & Diffie-Hellman)\n3.11. - Python 3 (Advanced Loops, Tuples, Sets, Dicts)\n5.11. - Basic of Cryptography 3 (Public Key Crypto)\n10.11. - Python 4 (Exceptions, File Handling, Hashlib)\n12.11. - Basic of Cryptography 4 (Digital Signatures & PKI)\n17.11. -\nno lecture\n19.11. - Authentication\n24.11. - Python 5 (Importing, JSON, Requests)\n26.11. - Network Security 1 (LAN, WLAN, DHCP)\n1.12. - Python 6 (Regular Expressions)\n3.12. - Network Security 2 (IPv4, IPv6, BGP)\nFrom hereon in, no more lectures on Thursdays\n8.12. - Network Security 3 (UDP, TCP, Firewalls)\n15.12. - Network Security 4 (DNS)\n5.1. - Network Security 5 (Denial of Service, TOR)\n12.1. - Network Security 6 (TLS, HTTPS, Certificates)\n19.1. - Web Security 1 (Server-Side Security)\n26.1. - Web Security 2 (Client-Side Security)\n2.2. - Q/A & Exam Preparation\n16.2. - main exam (10-12)\n25.3. - backup exam (10-12)\nTutorials\nThe available time slots for tutorials are Friday 12-14, Monday 10-12 and Monday 12-14. All tutorials take place in the CISPA building (E9.1). The Friday 12-14 and Monday 10-12 tutorials are in room 0.02; the Monday 12-14 tutorial is in the lecture hall (Room 0.05).\nGrading and Exam information\nThere will be a final exam at the end of the semester, which will determine the course grade. To be eligible for the exam, and subsequently, to earn course credits, you need to score\nat least\n50% of the available points on all 12 exercise sheets, with a maximum of two sheets being allowed to be skipped,\nand\nachieve 50% of the points from the Python exercises.\nAny changes to this will be announced in the first lecture.\nRegistration\nYou can register for this course in the CMS until Wednesday, October 14, at 23:59.\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nLegal Notice\nIf you encounter technical problems, please contact\nthe administrators\n.",
