vacy, including\nusers' mental models of AI,\nprivacy concerns,\nvulnerable or marginalized groups,\ntechnology-facilitated abuse, scams, and misinformation.\nThe\ntechnical perspective\nexamines the security of AI, machine-learning, and large language model systems, including\nsecure code generation,\nthe offensive use of AI,\nrisks introduced by autonomous agents, and\nmethods for detecting generated media.\nStudents will engage with\nrecent scientific publications\n,\npresent one selected topic\n, and\nlead a critical discussion\nof its human and technical dimensions. Presentations should explain the underlying technology, examine relevant security and privacy concerns, consider how people understand and interact with the system, and discuss how proposed safeguards may fail in real-world settings.\nTopics\n#\nTopic\n1\nMental Models of AI\n2\nPrivacy in AI Chatbots\n3\nYouth, AI, and Privacy\n4\nAI-Facilitated Scams and Phishing\n5\nDeepfakes, Misinformation, and Authenticity\n6\nAI and Image-Based Sexual Abuse\n7\nOverreliance and Verification of AI Advice\n8\nAI Coding Assistants and Secure Development\n9\nAI Agents and Human Oversight\n10\nWorkplace AI and Organizational Security\n11\nBystander Privacy in AI Systems\n12\nMinorities, Fairness, and Unequal AI Harms\nSpecial Notes\nThis seminar does not include a written seminar paper. In light of the growing use of generative AI in writing, the course instead places particular emphasis on students' own understanding,\npresentation\n, critical reasoning, and\nactive participation in discussion\n. Assessment will therefore be based on presentations and contributions to seminar discussions.\nTalk Schedule (Tentative)\n#\nDate\nRoom\nMeeting\n-\nOctober 13, 2026\n-\nSeminar Assignment Week\n1\nOctober 20, 2026 - 2:00pm till 5:00pm\nCISPA (E9 1) - Room 0.02 Showroom\nKick-off - Humans & AI\n2\nOctober 27, 2026 - 2:00pm till 5:00pm\nCISPA (E9 1) - Room 0.02 Showroom\nHow to Read and Present Scientific Papers\n-\nNovember 3, 2026\n-\nNo Meeting - Preparation Time\n-\nNovember 10, 2026\n-\nNo Meeting - Preparation Time\n-\nNovember 17, 2026\n-\nNo Meeting - Preparation Time\n3\nNovember 24, 2026 - 2:00pm till 5:00pm\nCISPA (E9 1) - Room 0.02 Showroom\n2x Practice Talks + 2x Practice Talks\n4\nDecember 1, 2026 - 2:00pm till 5:00pm\nCISPA (E9 1) - Room 0.02 Showroom\n2x Practice Talks + 2x Practice Talks\n-\nDecember 8, 2026\n-\nNo Meeting - Preparation Time\n5\nDecember 15, 2026 - 2:00pm till 5:00pm\nCISPA (E9 1) - Room 0.02 Showroom\n2x Practice Talks + 2x Practice Talks\n-\nDecember 22, 2026\n-\nNo Meeting - Winter Break 🎅\n-\nDecember 29, 2026\n-\nNo Meeting - Winter Break 🎆\n-\nJanuary 5, 2027\n-\nNo Meeting - Preparation Time\n6\nJanuary 12, 2027 - 2:00pm till 5:00pm\nCISPA (E9 1) - Room 0.02 Showroom\n2x Final Talks + 2x Final Talks\n7\nJanuary 19, 2027 - 2:00pm till 5:00pm\nCISPA (E9 1) - Room 0.02 Showroom\n2x Final Talks + 2x Final Talks\n8\nJanuary 26, 2027 - 2:00pm till 5:00pm\nCISPA (E9 1) - Room 0.02 Showroom\n2x Final Talks + 2x Final Talks\n-\nFebruary 2, 2027\n-\nNo Meeting - Reserved: Backup\nTime and Location\nDate\n:\nThe seminar will take place on\nTuesdays\n,\nstarting\nOctober 20, 2026\n.\nTime\n:\n2-5pm\n(with a short break)\nLocation\n:\nBuilding\nE9 1\n,\nCISPA C0\n, Stuhlsatzenhaus 5, 66123 Saarbruecken.\nRoom: 0.02 Showroom\nLinks\n:\nSIC Seminars\nCourse Catalog\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nLegal Notice\nIf you encounter technical problems, please contact\nthe administrators\n.",
