    "text": "Main Page\nCybersecurity in Organizational Practice\nJonas Hielscher\nNews\nCurrently, no news are available\nCybersecurity in Organizational Practice\nTo\nregister\n, please apply for this seminar through the\ncentral seminar assignment system.\nWe are proud to announce that the 2025 version of this seminar was selected as Busy-Beaver runner-up, and hence voted as of the three best seminars by the student council!\nContent\nIn this seminar, we will\nlearn\nhow cybersecurity is practically implemented in organizations (enterprises, public agencies, NGOs, etc.) and discuss why academic cybersecurity concepts are often not followed in practice. We will\nread\nand discuss papers on cybersecurity in organizations, frequently utilizing human-centered research methods such as interviews, surveys, focus groups, and case studies.\nWe will\nread\nvarious recent scientific publications on cybersecurity in organizational practice and foundational papers, some of which have been around for over two decades. We will\ndiscuss\nthose papers in the seminar based on\npresentations\nby student teams. Throughout the seminar, we will\nreflect\nupon our own (current and future) experience with cybersecurity in organizational practice. We will\nlearn\nto negotiate cybersecurity strategies with other stakeholders in our future professions.\nTopics might include\nOrganizational Security Research Methods,\nRegulations, Norms, and Frameworks,\nVarious Roles in Organizational Security,\nHuman-Centered Security,\nEconomics of Information Security,\nOrganizational (Security) Leadership, Change Management, Communication,\nSecure Software Development in Organizations, and\nHow to Find and Read Scientific Papers.\nTime & Location\nThe seminar will take place on\nTuesdays from 10:15 to 11:45\n. There will be irregular seminar meetings, where there will be lecture-style teaching, group discussions, presentations, etc. The exact schedule will be discussed at the seminar start. As the grading will happen during these sessions you can only sign up if you are available on all Tuesdays in the semester.\nThe\nkick-off session will take place on October 20th at 10:15 in TBA.\nLocation\n: TBA\nTasks & Grading\nGrading will be based on (group) presentations, discussion participation, and further hand-ins.\nRegular attendance is required to pass the seminar.\nRegistration & Prerequisites\nAll students must register using the\ncentral seminar assignment system.\nThere are no formal prerequisites for this course. However, to succeed in this seminar, you should consider the following:\nYou should be interested in perfecting your presentation skills. Throughout the seminar, you will give multiple (smaller) presentations, and we expect you to progress in your skills over time.\nYou should be interested in learning to read and understand a variety of research papers, their methods, and their limitations, and you should be willing to discuss this.\nYou should be interested in questioning your position and approach to cybersecurity and able to consider the perspectives of various organizational stakeholders.\nYou must be interested in interdisciplinary perspectives on cybersecurity, expanding the mathematical and engineering approach to a more human-centered perspective.\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nLegal Notice\nIf you encounter technical problems, please contact\nthe administrators\n.",
