he permission of its owners and may not use anything you learn in this class for evil. If you have any doubts about whether or not something you want to do is ethical and legal, you should check with the course instructor before proceeding.\nIn this course, generative AI tools are viewed as powerful learning aids. You are encouraged to use them ethically to brainstorm ideas or refine the structure of your writing. However, AI should supplement\nyour learning, not replace it. You are ultimately responsible for the accuracy, logic, and integrity of the work you submit. To ensure transparency, your final written report must include an\nAI Disclosure Statement\n. Select the option below that applies (and you are encouraged to add more details):\nOption A: No AI Used.\n\"No generative AI tools were used in the conception, literature review, or writing of this report.\"\nOption B: AI Used for Assistance.\n\"I utilized [name of the tool] to assist with [specific tasks]. All final analysis and writing were completed and verified by the author.\"\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nLegal Notice\nIf you encounter technical problems, please contact\nthe administrators\n.",
