    "title": "Main Page",
    "text": "Main Page\nSecurity (WS 2026/2027)\nNils Ole Tippenhauer\nRegistration for this course\nis open until\nFriday, 30.10.2026 23:59\n.\nNews\nCurrently, no news are available\nSecurity\nThe Security core lecture (\"Stammvorlesung\") will be offered in the winter term 2026/2027.\nLectures\nWe plan to offer the lecture as a in-person class. Note: First lecture will be on October 14 with an Introduction. The main lecture content starts in the second week. In general, classes will be in-person.\nThe schedule for the two lectures per week is as follows:\nMonday 12:15-13:45 (GHH, E 2.2)\nWednesday 12:15-13:45 (GHH, E2.2)\nRegistration\nRegistration in this CMS is required until October 31, 2026. LSF exam registration is required to participate in the exams (and will be possible until 1 week before the final exam). Please contact your Prüfungsamt for any problems with LSF registrations. Only for Erasmus students a registration solely on CMS is sufficient. Any other student cannot write the exam unless registered on LSF. We cannot register you on LSF. We will remove any CMS registrations for students that are not qualified (due to missing exercise points) or missing LSF registration.\nTutorials\nTutorial 1\nMonday 10:00-12:00\n0.07, E9 1\nTutorial 2\nWednesday 16:00-18:00\nSR 016 in E1 3\nTutorial 3\nWednesday 10:00-12:00\nSR 016 in E1 3\nTutorial 4\nFriday 10:00-12:00\n0.07, E9 1\nTutorial 5\nTuesday 10:00-12:00\n0.07, E9 1\nOffice Hour\nMonday 16:00-18:00  - SR 013 in E1 3\nExams\nScheduled for:\nFinal: 19.02.27 14:00 - 16:00h\nRe-exam: 18.03.27 14:00 - 16:00h\nLocation: We will have GHH and 2 lecture halls in E1 3 (001 and 003) for both exams. Room assignment for students will be done via CMS shortly before the exam.\nMental Health\nBeing a student is challenging and might be very overwhelming. If you need support during times of struggle, reach out to friends, family, or faculty you trust. The student union at UdS also offers a\ncounseling service\nthat you may contact. You do not have to go through this alone! If for whatever reason (e.g., a personal emergency) you cannot attend the lectures or deliver your work in time, please let us know and we will make appropriate arrangements.\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nLegal Notice\nIf you encounter technical problems, please contact\nthe administrators\n.",
