    "title": "Block Seminar Machine Learning for Language Processing (Spring 2027) – Spoken Language Systems",
    "text": "Block Seminar Machine Learning for Language Processing (Spring 2027) – Spoken Language Systems\nSkip to content\nDeep learning is the predominant machine learning paradigm in language processing. This approach not only gave huge performance improvements across a large variety of natural language processing tasks. This time we will loke at agentic AI for lifes science and other papers on drug discovery\nLecturer:\nDietrich Klakow\nLocation:\nt.d.b\nTime\n: block course in the spring break 2027 however preparations start earlier. Here the specific time line\nClosing topic doodle: tbd\nKick-Off: tbd\nOne page outline: tbd\nDraft presentation: tbd\nPractice talks and final talks will be during the spring break. Time/date will be decided during the kick-off.\nApplication for participation:\nsee CS seminar system (for CS; BioInf, DSAI, VC, ES, …), for CoLI,LST, LCT use LSF to apply.\nLSF exam registration deadline:\n29.1.27\nGrading (tentative):\n5%  three slide/5 min presentation\n10% draft of full presentation\n10% practice talk\n25% own experiments and coding\n10% report on coding task\n35% final talk\n5% contributions to discussion during final talk of fellow participants\nList of Topics (tentative):\nAugmenting large language models with chemistry tools\nAutonomous chemical research with large language models\nLIDDIA: Language-based Intelligent Drug Discovery Agent\nDrugAgent: Automating AI-aided Drug Discovery Programming through LLM Multi-Agent Collaboration\nDemocratising real-world drug discovery through agentic AI\nTowards an AI co-scientist\nAI agents in drug discovery: applications and case studies\nTowards end-to-end automation of AI research\nDeCoDe: Decoupling Binding Position and Molecular Conformation in 3D Ligand Diffusion for Structure-Based Drug Design\nFrom Feasible to Practical: Pareto-Optimal Synthesis Planning\nContrastive Geometric Learning Unlocks Unified Structure- and Ligand-Based Drug Design\nLearning Hamiltonian Flow Maps: Mean Flow Consistency for Large-Timestep Molecular Dynamics\nThe rise of agentic AI in drug discovery from static tools to autonomous virtual scientists\nChain-of-Molecules: Agentic Reasoning in Chemical Space for Constrained Molecular Optimization",
    "error": ""
