    "title": "Lecture schedule",
    "text": "Lecture schedule\nSystems Security\nAli Abbasi, Moritz Schloegel\nLecture schedule\nThe following schedule provides an overview of the planned topics for all lectures. Note that unexpected circumstances may require changes to the plan.\nLecture\nDate\nTopic\nInfo\nInstructor\n1\nOctober 23\nIntro\nAdministrative aspects and introduction\nAli\n2\nOctober 30\nx86 assembly I\nx86/x64 introduction\nMoritz\n3\nNovember 6\nx86 assembly II\nx86/x64 introduction\nMoritz\n4\nNovember 13\nReverse Engineering\nControl + data structure recovery\nMoritz\n5\nNovember 20\nSoftware Security I\nBuffer overflows and Co.\nMoritz\n6\nNovember 27\nSoftware Security II\nDefenses and more vulnerabilities\nMoritz\n7\nDecember 4\nSoftware Security III\nROP / CFI / other defenses\nAli\n8\nDecember 11\nMidterm\nAli\n9\nDecember 18\nSoftware Security IV\nOther kinds of vulnerabilities\nAli\n10\nJanuary 8\nARM Assembly\nIntro to ARM Assembly\nAli\n11\nJanuary 15\nHeap Security I\nAttacks on heap data structures\nAli\n12\nJanuary 22\nHeap Security II\nAttacks on heap data structures\nAli\n13\nJanuary 29\nSoftware Testing\nFuzzing\nAddison Crump (guest lecture)\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nLegal Notice\nIf you encounter technical problems, please contact\nthe administrators\n.",
